  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...    \nThrough the middle of the upcoming work week, following the \ndeparture of this dynamic weekend system, we can expect dry \nconditions, and transient upper level ridging, resulting in \ntemperatures slowly warming closer to seasonal levels (despite \ndaytime highs likely remaining a few degrees below the daily \nnormals). By late week, ensembles diverge considerably with \nrespect to another upper low/positively tilted shortwave trough \npossibly impacting the region. Some solutions show quasi-zonal \nflow taking shape over the Southwest US after the transient \nridging shifts east of the area, while others show a shortwave \ndisturbance capable of diving well south of the region and \nresulting in a brief moisture return. Regardless of the outcome, \nfairly benign conditions seem to be the most likely outcome. The \ntrajectory of the late week system is not favorable for rain \nchances, its residence time too short for better quality moisture \nto be pulled into the area, and if it remains an open wave, its \npositive tilt does not bode well for providing upper level support\nfor precipitation. NBM PoPs become introduced to the eastern AZ \nhigh terrain on the order of 15-25% Friday as a result, but we \nshould not put too much stock in this, as the forecast remains \nhighly uncertain at this time.",
